From: MilkFlint <milkflint@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: wake the interface's txq on its own AC's
 pass

__ieee80211_wake_txqs() runs once per AC. For the interface's own txq
(multicast and broadcast) it cleared the dirty mark before checking that
the pass is for that txq's AC, so the voice pass, which runs first, used
up the mark of the best-effort txq without waking it, and the best-effort
pass then found nothing to wake. Multicast queued while the queues were
stopped (a flush, a channel switch, a restart) waited for the next wake-up
from other traffic.

Check the AC first.

---
--- a/net/mac80211/util.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/util.c
@@ -369,8 +369,13 @@ static void __ieee80211_wake_txqs(struct ieee80211_sub
 
 	txqi = to_txq_info(vif->txq);
 
-	if (!test_and_clear_bit(IEEE80211_TXQ_DIRTY, &txqi->flags) ||
-	    (ps && atomic_read(&ps->num_sta_ps)) || ac != vif->txq->ac)
+	/*
+	 * Check the AC first: this runs once per AC, and clearing the bit
+	 * on another AC's pass would lose the wake-up.
+	 */
+	if (ac != vif->txq->ac ||
+	    !test_and_clear_bit(IEEE80211_TXQ_DIRTY, &txqi->flags) ||
+	    (ps && atomic_read(&ps->num_sta_ps)))
 		goto out;
 
 	spin_unlock(&fq->lock);
